WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:02.130
 We're going to make a
bit of an island favorite,

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.150
and that's the mojito.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.040
You don't want to tear
the hell out of the mint.

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.873
We want to agitate it
a bit, so just give it

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:08.700
a quick slap over
the back of your hand

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:10.920
because what we want to
have is that first bouquet

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.410
as you go to take a sip.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.540
 I'm Lynnette Marrero.

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:15.790
 And I'm Ryan Chetiyawardana.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.340
I think I messed up
my own name there.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:17.840
[LAUGHTER]

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.800
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.800
To me, cocktails are magic, and
there's something about them

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.050
that really helps bring together
people in a wonderful way.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:26.970
[CORK POPS]

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:30.400
 I've learned how to find
expression through liquid arts,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.759
so I hope you get
extremely creative.

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:34.410
The foundation for
all good cocktails

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.120
comes from knowing
classic cocktails.

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:36.800
 Whiskey sour.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.300
 Martini.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.070
 The Bloody Mary.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:38.610
 Margarita.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.390
 The Old Fashioned.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:41.182
 Understanding the
balance of those drinks

00:00:41.182 --> 00:00:42.403
is extremely important.

00:00:42.403 --> 00:00:44.070
 I want to show how
great cocktails can

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.507
fit into your everyday life.

00:00:46.507 --> 00:00:47.340
[RATTLING ICE CUBES]

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.705
 It's hard not to be inspired
by a charcuterie plate.

00:00:49.705 --> 00:00:52.070
 One of my favorite pairings
is having a smoky whiskey

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:52.940
with blue cheese.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.003
That's a great
flavor combination.

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:56.670
Bitters are the
seasoning of your drink.

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:58.910
They're there to kind of bridge
all the other flavors together,

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.650
and it really acts
as this kind of base

00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:01.942
in the background of the drink.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:03.500
Really simple, but
super delicious.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.800
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.970
 Knowing how to incorporate
eggs into a drink safely

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:10.778
and deliciously is
really important.

00:01:10.778 --> 00:01:12.570
You have to think about
it in bakery terms.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:14.310
You're using
something that is raw

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.990
that is getting
cooked by the citrus.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.390
That's what creates
that silky texture.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.160
 It's not about
having crazy equipment.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.110
Ultimately, you can
make things using

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:25.260
jam jars or teapots or
paintbrushes and chopsticks

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.130
to stir your drinks.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:28.150
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.270
 No matter what
your background is,

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:32.650
I guarantee we will learn
some things together.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:33.630
 And there's
something really fun

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.280
about getting your
friends together and just

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.572
throwing this all into the mix.

00:01:36.572 --> 00:01:38.220
 Cocktails and bars
have always been

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:41.250
a place where people come
together to share ideas,

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:44.490
and so we are thrilled
to share our ideas,

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:47.190
our philosophies, our sense
of community with you.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:47.970
Cheers.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:48.510
 Cheers.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:49.860
Always a pleasure.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.190
I'm Ryan Chetiyawardana.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.905
 I am Lynnette Marrero.

00:01:52.905 --> 00:01:54.480
 And this is our MasterClass.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:57.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

